 "note": "TEAM PLAY 2V2 (the rewritten tutorial, TUTORIAL-REWRITE-DESIGN.md sec3/5c). Seats A and C are the allies on the left (A the player's home H at the top, C the ally's home A at the bottom), B and D the rivals on the right (BH1 top, BH2 bottom): the Alpha 11 classics' convention. A small triangle lattice of short decks, mirrored left/right and top/bottom, no relay, no Last Stand. S is the shared node: one short deck from both allied homes (and from N1, N2 and the T2 centre C), at least 3 decks from either rival home - the lesson's shared garrison, ownership handover and EJECT happen there. BS is the rivals' mirror of S. Names: H (seat A home), A (ally C home), S (shared node), N1 / N2 (the T1 nodes on the top and bottom lanes), C (T2 centre), B1 / B2, BS, BH1 (seat B home), BH2 (seat D home).",
